export default {"id":"m4l-level-15","number":15,"title":"Module 15","skillBand":"Textbook","duration":"From the course textbook","summary":"15.1","modules":[{"id":"m4l-m-15-1-1","code":"15.1","title":"15.1","blurb":"15.1","outcomes":[],"sources":[],"practiceFocus":[],"checkpoints":[],"lessons":[{"id":"m4l-l-15-1-1","title":"15.1.1: Live 12 MIDI Tools Architecture and Lifecycle","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"1. Metadata and Prerequisites","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["<strong>Lesson ID:</strong> Lesson 15.1.1","<strong>Module / Section:</strong> Module 15 / Section 15.1","<strong>Track:</strong> <code>m4l-devices</code>","<strong>Target Environment:</strong> Ableton Live 12 Standard (with Max for Live add-on) / Live 12 Suite; bundled Cycling '74 Max 9 runtime.","<strong>Operating Systems:</strong> Windows, macOS.","<strong>Prerequisites:</strong> Lesson 14.3.1 - Node for Max Architecture and Boundaries.","<strong>Primary Sources:</strong>","Ableton Live 12 Reference Manual: Chapter 31 (<em>Max for Live</em>) &amp; <em>MIDI Tools</em>.","Cycling '74: <em>Max for Live MIDI Tools Guide (<code>live_miditools</code>)</em>.","Ableton Production Guidelines: <em>Live 12 MIDI Tools Standards</em>."],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"2. Learning Objectives","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"By the conclusion of this module, the student will be able to:"},{"type":"list","items":["Explain the architectural role of <strong>Live 12 MIDI Tools</strong> as Clip View integrated editors, contrasting them with track-chain MIDI effects.","Differentiate between <strong>MIDI Transformation Tools</strong> (mutating existing clip notes) and <strong>MIDI Generative Tools</strong> (synthesizing new note patterns from scratch).","Adhere to mandatory Live 12 User Library directory structures for Transformations and Generators.","Trigger host library indexing to ensure user-authored MIDI Tools appear in Clip View dropdown selectors.","Ingest and edit default Max for Live MIDI Tool templates."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"3. Architectural and Theoretical Foundations","blocks":[{"type":"heading","text":"3.1 Clip View Integration Model","level":3},{"type":"prose","html":"Prior to Live 12, all Max for Live devices existed exclusively in track device chains. Live 12 introduced a dedicated integration surface directly within <strong>Clip View</strong>:"},{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                        LIVE 12 MIDI TOOLS HOST TOPOLOGY                       |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                                                                               |\n|  [ Ableton Live 12 Clip View (Piano Roll Editor) ]                            |\n|       |                                                                       |\n|       +---&gt; [ Transformations Panel ]                                         |\n|       |     - Houses Transformation Tools (.amxd)                             |\n|       |     - Modifies selected notes or entire clip note arrays              |\n|       |       (Quantize, Velocity Arcs, Strum, Time Warp)                     |\n|       |                                                                       |\n|       +---&gt; [ Generators Panel ]                                              |\n|             - Houses Generative Tools (.amxd)                                 |\n|             - Creates new note data into empty or selected clip slots         |\n|               (Euclidean rhythms, Melodic generators, Chord stacks)           |\n|                                                                               |\n|  *Note:* MIDI Tools do NOT process real-time streaming audio or MIDI cords.   |\n|  They execute batch operations on structured JSON/Dictionary note data!       |\n|                                                                               |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+</pre>"}]},{"type":"step","title":"4. File Storage and Library Indexing Requirements","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Ableton Live 12 discovers and exposes MIDI Tools in Clip View menus based strictly on <strong>file system location</strong>:"},{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">User Library/\n└── MIDI Tools/\n    ├── Transformations/   &lt;-- Transformation Tools (.amxd) MUST be stored here!\n    └── Generators/        &lt;-- Generative Tools (.amxd) MUST be stored here!</pre>"},{"type":"heading","text":"4.1 The Live Indexer Rule","level":3},{"type":"list","items":["If an <code>.amxd</code> MIDI tool is saved in an arbitrary desktop folder or standard audio effect directory, <strong>Live 12 will not index it</strong>, and it will not appear in the Clip View selector menus.","<strong>Custom Folder Inclusion:</strong> If devices reside outside the User Library, the containing parent directory must be added as an indexed shortcut under <strong>Places</strong> in Live's browser."],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"5. Editing and Template Ingestion","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"To author a custom MIDI Tool:"},{"type":"list","items":["In Live 12, open Clip View on any MIDI clip.","Navigate to the <strong>Transformations</strong> or <strong>Generators</strong> tab.","Select any default Max for Live MIDI Tool (e.g., <em>Velocity Shaper</em> or <em>Euclidean</em>).","Right-click the tool header → select <strong>Edit in Max</strong>.","The editor instantiates the specialized MIDI Tool template containing <code>[live.miditool.in]</code> and <code>[live.miditool.out]</code>."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"6. Laboratory Exercise","blocks":[{"type":"heading","text":"Objective","level":3},{"type":"prose","html":"Duplicate a default Transformation tool template using Save As, locate it in the correct User Library path, and verify that Live indexes and displays the custom tool in Clip View."},{"type":"heading","text":"Step-by-Step Procedure","level":3},{"type":"list","items":["In Ableton Live 12, create an empty MIDI Track and create a 1-bar MIDI Clip.","Double-click the clip to open Clip View.","Select the <strong>Transformations</strong> tab in the clip sidebar.","Choose any Max Transformation tool from the selector dropdown.","Right-click the tool header and select <strong>Edit in Max</strong>.","In the Max editor, select <strong>File</strong> → <strong>Save As...</strong>.","Name the file <code>Custom_Velocity_Transform.amxd</code>.","Save into the exact directory: <code>User Library/MIDI Tools/Transformations/</code>","Close the Max editor.","Return to Live 12: In Clip View, open the Transformations dropdown selector.","Confirm that <code>Custom_Velocity_Transform</code> appears in the list and loads into Clip View."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"7. Common Pitfalls and Failure Modes","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["<strong>Saving Tools in Standard MIDI Effect Folders:</strong> Saving a MIDI Tool into <code>Presets/MIDI Effects/</code>. Live will treat the file as a track-chain processor; it will fail to load in Clip View and will error if dragged onto a track.","<strong>Attempting Track-Chain Insertion:</strong> Dragging a MIDI Tool <code>.amxd</code> onto a track mixer strip. MIDI Tools cannot execute as track effects and will be rejected by Live's chain manager.","<strong>Patcher Corruption from Deleting I/O Objects:</strong> Deleting <code>[live.miditool.in]</code> or <code>[live.miditool.out]</code> from the template. MIDI Tools require these dedicated objects to interface with Live's clip database."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"8. Self-Assessment & Checkpoint","blocks":[{"type":"heading","text":"Checkpoint Criteria","level":3},{"type":"prose","html":"To confirm mastery of this module, the student must successfully complete the following criteria:"},{"type":"list","items":["[ ] Differentiate between a MIDI Transformation Tool and a MIDI Generative Tool in Live 12.","[ ] Specify the exact filesystem paths where Transformation and Generative <code>.amxd</code> tools must be saved.","[ ] Demonstrate opening the Max editor from within Live 12's Clip View panel."],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"9. Source Citations","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Ableton AG. (2024). <em>Ableton Live 12 Reference Manual: MIDI Tools &amp; Clip View Integration</em>. Berlin: Ableton AG.","Cycling '74. (2024). <em>Max for Live MIDI Tools Architecture Guide (<code>live_miditools</code>)</em>. San Francisco: Cycling '74.","Ableton AG. (2023). <em>Max for Live Production Guidelines: Live 12 Tool Standards</em>. Ableton Developer Documentation."],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8}],"exercises":[]},{"id":"m4l-m-15-2-2","code":"15.2","title":"15.2","blurb":"15.2","outcomes":[],"sources":[],"practiceFocus":[],"checkpoints":[],"lessons":[{"id":"m4l-l-15-2-1","title":"15.2.1: Note Dictionaries and Data Flow","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"1. Metadata and Prerequisites","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["<strong>Lesson ID:</strong> Lesson 15.2.1","<strong>Module / Section:</strong> Module 15 / Section 15.2","<strong>Track:</strong> <code>m4l-devices</code>","<strong>Target Environment:</strong> Ableton Live 12 Standard (with Max for Live add-on) / Live 12 Suite; bundled Cycling '74 Max 9 runtime.","<strong>Operating Systems:</strong> Windows, macOS.","<strong>Prerequisites:</strong> Lesson 15.1.1 - Live 12 MIDI Tools Architecture and Lifecycle.","<strong>Primary Sources:</strong>","Cycling '74: <em>Max for Live Reference: live.miditool.in and live.miditool.out</em>.","Cycling '74: <em>Max 9 Dictionary (dict) Guide: Note Schema</em>.","Ableton Production Guidelines: <em>Deterministic Seeding in MIDI Tools</em>."],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"2. Learning Objectives","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"By the conclusion of this module, the student will be able to:"},{"type":"list","items":["Parse and manipulate note lists and clip metadata using <code>[live.miditool.in]</code> and <code>[live.miditool.out]</code>.","Navigate the official <strong>Live 12 Note Dictionary Schema</strong> (<code>pitch</code>, <code>start_time</code>, <code>duration</code>, <code>velocity</code>, <code>probability</code>, <code>velocity_deviation</code>).","Differentiate between Transformation control flow (ingesting incoming notes, mutating properties, outputting transformed dictionary) and Generative control flow (synthesizing notes from empty state).","Apply the <strong>Mandatory Determinism Rule</strong>: Re-seeding all stochastic / random generators with explicit user-defined seeds before note generation.","Guarantee repeated trigger stability when applying tools across variable selection ranges."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"3. The live.miditool I/O Pipeline and Note Dictionary Schema","blocks":[{"type":"heading","text":"3.1 The Dataflow Pipeline","level":3},{"type":"prose","html":"Unlike track effects which receive serial byte streams, MIDI Tools operate on discrete hierarchical dictionaries (<code>dict</code>):"},{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                       MIDI TOOL DICTIONARY PIPELINE                           |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                                                                               |\n|  [ live.miditool.in ]                                                         |\n|       |                                                                       |\n|       +---&gt; Outlet 1: [ dictionary &lt;dict_name&gt; ] (Full Clip / Note Selection) |\n|       |                                                                       |\n|       +---&gt; Outlet 2: [ bang ] (Trigger on Apply / Parameter Adjustment)      |\n|                                                                               |\n|  [ Internal Dictionary Processing Pipeline ]                                  |\n|  - Parse \"notes\" array using [dict.unpack] or JavaScript                      |\n|  - Mutate pitch, time, duration, velocity                                     |\n|  - Re-pack into target dictionary                                             |\n|                                                                               |\n|  [ live.miditool.out ]                                                        |\n|       ^                                                                       |\n|       | (Inlet: Modified or Generated Dictionary)                             |\n|  (Live 12 writes the updated note structure directly into the MIDI clip!)     |\n|                                                                               |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+</pre>"},{"type":"heading","text":"3.2 The Live 12 Note Dictionary Schema","level":3},{"type":"prose","html":"Every individual note inside the <code>notes</code> array conforms to the following schema:"},{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">{\n  \"notes\": [\n    {\n      \"pitch\": 60,\n      \"start_time\": 0.0,\n      \"duration\": 0.25,\n      \"velocity\": 100.0,\n      \"probability\": 1.0,\n      \"velocity_deviation\": 0.0,\n      \"release_velocity\": 64.0\n    }\n  ]\n}</pre>"},{"type":"list","items":["<strong><code>pitch</code> (Int):</strong> MIDI Note Number (0–127).","<strong><code>start_time</code> (Float):</strong> Note onset position measured in fractional beats from clip start (0.0 = Bar 1 Beat 1).","<strong><code>duration</code> (Float):</strong> Note length in beats (1.0 = Quarter Note, 0.25 = Sixteenth Note).","<strong><code>velocity</code> (Float):</strong> Note velocity (1.0–127.0).","<strong><code>probability</code> (Float):</strong> Playback chance (0.0–1.0, where 1.0 = 100%)."],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"4. The Mandatory Determinism and Seeding Rule","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"According to the <strong>Ableton Production Guidelines Final Checklist</strong>:"},{"type":"callout","variant":"key","title":"Note","html":"<em>\"Generative and probabilistic MIDI Tools must be completely deterministic. When a user clicks 'Apply' or adjusts a parameter, the tool must produce the identical note output every time unless the user explicitly alters the Random Seed parameter.\"</em>"},{"type":"heading","text":"Why Determinism is Mandatory:","level":3},{"type":"prose","html":"In Live 12, adjusting any slider on a generative MIDI Tool causes the tool to re-execute in real-time to provide interactive visual feedback in the piano roll."},{"type":"list","items":["If the generator uses un-seeded <code>[random]</code>, moving a slider causes notes to jump randomly and chaotically on every mouse pixel movement.","When re-seeded with a fixed seed (<code>seed $1</code>), dragging a parameter scales values smoothly and predictably."],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"5. Laboratory Exercise","blocks":[{"type":"heading","text":"Objective","level":3},{"type":"prose","html":"Construct a Live 12 MIDI Transformation Tool that ingests selected clip notes, applies a velocity ramp slope across time, and writes the updated dictionary back to Clip View."},{"type":"heading","text":"Step-by-Step Procedure","level":3},{"type":"list","items":["In Live 12, open a Transformation template in Max and enable <strong>Open in Presentation</strong>.","Locate <code>[live.miditool.in]</code> and <code>[live.miditool.out]</code>.","Create a <code>[live.dial]</code> named <code>Velocity_Slope</code> (Float, <code>-64.0 to +64.0</code>, Initial: <code>0.0</code>).","Route the dictionary outlet of <code>[live.miditool.in]</code> to a JavaScript processor: <code>[js velocity_ramp.js]</code>.","Enter the following code into <code>velocity_ramp.js</code>:"],"ordered":true},{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">// velocity_ramp.js\nautowatch = 1;\n\nvar slope = 0.0;\n\nfunction set_slope(val) {\n    slope = val;\n}\n\nfunction dictionary(dictName) {\n    var d = new Dict(dictName);\n    var notes = d.get(\"notes\");\n    \n    if (!notes) return;\n    \n    // Ensure array format for single-note selections\n    if (!Array.isArray(notes)) {\n        notes = [notes];\n    }\n    \n    var noteCount = notes.length;\n    if (noteCount &lt; 2) {\n        outlet(0, \"dictionary\", dictName);\n        return;\n    }\n    \n    // Apply linear velocity ramp across note array\n    for (var i = 0; i &lt; noteCount; i++) {\n        var progress = i / (noteCount - 1); // 0.0 to 1.0\n        var velOffset = slope * (progress - 0.5) * 2.0;\n        var currentVel = notes[i].get(\"velocity\");\n        var newVel = Math.min(127, Math.max(1, currentVel + velOffset));\n        \n        notes[i].set(\"velocity\", newVel);\n    }\n    \n    outlet(0, \"dictionary\", dictName);\n}</pre>"},{"type":"list","items":["Connect <code>[live.dial Velocity_Slope]</code> → <code>[set_slope 1(</code>\\rightarrow$ <code>[js velocity_ramp.js]</code>.","Connect outlet 0 of <code>[js]</code> → inlet of <code>[live.miditool.out]</code>.","Save as <code>Velocity_Ramp_Transform.amxd</code> in <code>User Library/MIDI Tools/Transformations/</code>.","In Live 12, select a phrase of 16th notes in a MIDI clip.","Adjust <code>Velocity_Slope</code>: Observe the piano roll velocities ramping upward or downward in real time."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"6. Common Pitfalls and Failure Modes","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["<strong>Un-seeded Randomness Causing UI Jitter:</strong> Building generative tools using free-running random numbers, causing notes in Clip View to flicker wildly during slider adjustments. Always seed random generators.","<strong>Single-Note Array Truncation Bug:</strong> Forgetting that <code>Dict.get(\"notes\")</code> returns an Object instead of an Array when only a single note is selected. Always verify <code>Array.isArray(notes)</code>.","<strong>Invalid Note Range Overflows:</strong> Writing pitch numbers &lt; 0 or &gt; 127 into the note dictionary, resulting in silent note rejections by Live's clip database."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"7. Self-Assessment & Checkpoint","blocks":[{"type":"heading","text":"Checkpoint Criteria","level":3},{"type":"prose","html":"To confirm mastery of this module, the student must successfully complete the following criteria:"},{"type":"list","items":["[ ] Detail the five core properties required for every note entry in the Live 12 Note Dictionary.","[ ] Explain why deterministic pseudo-random seeding is mandatory in all generative MIDI Tools.","[ ] Connect <code>[live.miditool.in]</code> through a dictionary mutation network to <code>[live.miditool.out]</code>."],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"8. Source Citations","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Cycling '74. (2024). <em>Max for Live MIDI Tools Guide: Dictionary Schema and Dataflow</em>. San Francisco: Cycling '74.","Ableton AG. (2024). <em>Ableton Live 12 Reference Manual: MIDI Tools Data Architecture</em>. Berlin: Ableton AG.","Ableton AG. (2023). <em>Max for Live Production Guidelines: Deterministic Seeding Rules</em>. Ableton Developer Documentation."],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8}],"exercises":[]},{"id":"m4l-m-15-3-3","code":"15.3","title":"15.3","blurb":"15.3","outcomes":[],"sources":[],"practiceFocus":[],"checkpoints":[],"lessons":[{"id":"m4l-l-15-3-1","title":"15.3.1: MIDI Tool UX, Parameters, and Edge Cases","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"1. Metadata and Prerequisites","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["<strong>Lesson ID:</strong> Lesson 15.3.1 (Includes Gate K Assessment)","<strong>Module / Section:</strong> Module 15 / Section 15.3","<strong>Track:</strong> <code>m4l-devices</code>","<strong>Target Environment:</strong> Ableton Live 12 Standard (with Max for Live add-on) / Live 12 Suite; bundled Cycling '74 Max 9 runtime.","<strong>Operating Systems:</strong> Windows, macOS.","<strong>Prerequisites:</strong> Lesson 15.2.1 - Note Dictionaries and Data Flow (<code>live.miditool.*</code>).md).","<strong>Primary Sources:</strong>","Ableton Live 12 Reference Manual: <em>MIDI Tools UX Standards</em>.","Ableton Production Guidelines: <em>Live 12 Tool Parameter Hygiene</em>.","Cycling '74: <em>Max for Live MIDI Tools: Interface Design and Edge Cases</em>."],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"2. Learning Objectives","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"By the conclusion of this module, the student will be able to:"},{"type":"list","items":["Design compact, clip-focused user interfaces optimized for Live 12's Clip View side panel.","Apply parameter hygiene (Long Names, Short Names, Annotations, Initial Values) to MIDI Tools.","Establish default factory parameter states that immediately demonstrate tool functionality upon first opening.","Handle critical edge cases: completely empty clips, multi-bar selections, non-standard time signatures, and single-note selections.","Complete <strong>Gate K (MIDI Tools Mastery)</strong> by authoring, testing, and archiving one Transformation Tool and one Generative Tool."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"3. Clip View UI Constraints and Design Standards","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Inside Live 12's Clip View, vertical and horizontal real estate is strictly constrained:"},{"type":"list","items":["<strong>Panel Width:</strong> Fixed compact side panel (approximately 200–280 pixels wide).","<strong>Control Layout:</strong> Use vertical stacks of <code>live.dial</code>, <code>live.tab</code>, and <code>live.numbox</code> controls.","<strong>Instant Preview:</strong> Every parameter change must immediately emit a modified dictionary through <code>[live.miditool.out]</code> so the user sees notes update dynamically on the piano roll."],"ordered":false},{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                      CLIP VIEW TOOL INTERFACE GEOMETRY                        |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                                                                               |\n|  Live 12 Piano Roll (Right Side)          Clip View Tool Panel (Left Side)    |\n|  [ Note Grid: Bar 1 ... Bar 4 ]           +-----------------------------+     |\n|  [ ==   ==   ==   ==   ==     ]           | Tool: Euclidean Generator   |     |\n|                                           |                             |     |\n|                                           | [ Steps:  16              ] |     |\n|                                           | [ Pulses: 5               ] |     |\n|                                           | [ Rotate: 2               ] |     |\n|                                           | [ Seed:   104             ] |     |\n|                                           |                             |     |\n|                                           | [ (Apply Button)          ] |     |\n|                                           +-----------------------------+     |\n|                                                                               |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+</pre>"}]},{"type":"step","title":"4. Edge-Case Validation Matrix","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Every production-ready MIDI Tool must pass the following regression suite:"},{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                        MIDI TOOL REGRESSION TEST MATRIX                           |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------------+---------------------------+\n| Edge-Case Scenario| Expected Robust Behavior          | Failure Mode to Prevent   |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------------+---------------------------+\n| **Empty Clip**    | Tool generates notes or exits     | Patcher throws `null`     |\n|                   | cleanly without console errors.   | dictionary exception.     |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------------+---------------------------+\n| **Single Note**   | Applies transformation to that    | Script crashes assuming   |\n| **Selection**     | single note correctly.            | `notes` is always array.  |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------------+---------------------------+\n| **Multi-Bar Clip**| Scales operations across entire   | Tool hardcodes math       |\n| **(e.g., 32 Bars)**| selection length dynamically.     | assuming 1-bar length.    |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------------+---------------------------+\n| **3/4, 5/4, 7/8** | Respects clip time signature grid | Rhythms drift off beat    |\n| **Time Signatures**| and bar boundaries.               | boundaries.               |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------------+---------------------------+</pre>"}]},{"type":"step","title":"5. Laboratory Exercise","blocks":[{"type":"heading","text":"Objective","level":3},{"type":"prose","html":"Construct a production-ready <strong>Euclidean Rhythm MIDI Generator</strong> featuring Step Count, Pulse Count, Rotation, Velocity, Pitch, and Deterministic Seed parameters."},{"type":"heading","text":"Step-by-Step Procedure","level":3},{"type":"list","items":["In Live 12, open a Generator template in Max and enable <strong>Open in Presentation</strong>.","Locate <code>[live.miditool.in]</code> and <code>[live.miditool.out]</code>.","Create Parameter Controls:","<code>[live.numbox Steps]</code> (Int, <code>1 to 32</code>, Initial: <code>16</code>)","<code>[live.numbox Pulses]</code> (Int, <code>1 to 32</code>, Initial: <code>5</code>)","<code>[live.numbox Rotation]</code> (Int, <code>0 to 31</code>, Initial: <code>0</code>)","<code>[live.numbox Pitch]</code> (Int, <code>0 to 127</code>, Initial: <code>36</code> / C1 Kick)","<code>[live.dial Seed]</code> (Int, <code>1 to 9999</code>, Initial: <code>101</code>)","Ingest Parameters into JavaScript Euclidean Generator: <code>[js euclidean_gen.js]</code>.","Enter the following Euclidean distribution algorithm:"],"ordered":true},{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">// euclidean_gen.js\nautowatch = 1;\n\nvar steps = 16;\nvar pulses = 5;\nvar rotation = 0;\nvar pitch = 36;\n\nfunction set_steps(v) { steps = Math.max(1, v); generate(); }\nfunction set_pulses(v) { pulses = Math.min(steps, Math.max(0, v)); generate(); }\nfunction set_rotation(v) { rotation = v; generate(); }\nfunction set_pitch(v) { pitch = v; generate(); }\n\nfunction generate() {\n    var pattern = [];\n    var bucket = 0;\n    \n    // Bjorklund / Bresenham Euclidean Distribution\n    for (var i = 0; i &lt; steps; i++) {\n        bucket += pulses;\n        if (bucket &gt;= steps) {\n            bucket -= steps;\n            pattern.push(true);\n        } else {\n            pattern.push(false);\n        }\n    }\n    \n    // Apply Rotation\n    var rotated = [];\n    for (var r = 0; r &lt; steps; r++) {\n        rotated.push(pattern[(r + rotation) % steps]);\n    }\n    \n    // Construct Note Dictionary\n    var d = new Dict(\"generated_notes\");\n    var noteList = [];\n    var stepDuration = 4.0 / steps; // Assumes 1-bar 4/4\n    \n    for (var s = 0; s &lt; steps; s++) {\n        if (rotated[s]) {\n            var n = new Dict();\n            n.set(\"pitch\", pitch);\n            n.set(\"start_time\", s * stepDuration);\n            n.set(\"duration\", stepDuration * 0.8);\n            n.set(\"velocity\", 100.0);\n            n.set(\"probability\", 1.0);\n            noteList.push(n);\n        }\n    }\n    \n    d.set(\"notes\", noteList);\n    outlet(0, \"dictionary\", \"generated_notes\");\n}</pre>"},{"type":"list","items":["Connect <code>[js euclidean_gen.js]</code> outlet 0 → <code>[live.miditool.out]</code>.","Add parameters to Presentation Mode, stack vertically on the 8x8 grid (width: 220 px).","Save as <code>Euclidean_Generator.amxd</code> in <code>User Library/MIDI Tools/Generators/</code>.","In Live 12 Clip View, open the Generators panel: Select <code>Euclidean_Generator</code>.","Adjust Pulses and Steps: Observe the piano roll updating with mathematically perfect Euclidean rhythms instantly."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"6. Gate K Self-Assessment Checkpoint","blocks":[{"type":"callout","variant":"key","title":"Note","html":"[!IMPORTANT] <strong>Gate K: MIDI Tools Mastery Assessment</strong> To complete Module 15 and verify complete Live 12 MIDI Tool engineering proficiency, the student must execute and verify the following:"},{"type":"heading","text":"Practical Test Assignment:","level":3},{"type":"list","items":["<strong>Device 1: Velocity Ramp Transformation Tool (<code>Velocity_Ramp_Transform.amxd</code>):</strong>","Ingests selected notes via <code>[live.miditool.in]</code>.","Modifies velocity curves smoothly across arbitrary clip selections.","Passes single-note and empty clip tests with zero console errors.","<strong>Device 2: Euclidean Generative Tool (<code>Euclidean_Generator.amxd</code>):</strong>","Synthesizes rhythmic patterns into empty clips.","Implements deterministic seeding (zero jitter during slider moves).","Saved in <code>User Library/MIDI Tools/Generators/</code> and indexes in Clip View.","<strong>Universal Audit:</strong> Both tools must use <code>live.*</code> parameter objects, have full Info View annotations, and conform to the standard Clip View panel geometry."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"7. Common Pitfalls and Failure Modes","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["<strong>Horizontal Canvas Sprawl:</strong> Designing a 600-pixel wide interface for a MIDI Tool. The Clip View tool panel is narrow; horizontal sprawl forces clipped controls. Keep layouts under 240 pixels.","<strong>Failing to Re-generate on Parameter Move:</strong> Updating an internal variable without triggering <code>generate()</code> and <code>[live.miditool.out]</code>. The user will move sliders and see no change on the piano roll until they manually click elsewhere.","<strong>Zero-Division Crashes:</strong> Allowing <code>steps</code> to reach <code>0</code> in JavaScript, causing <code>division by zero</code> exceptions and freezing dictionary output."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"8. Source Citations","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Ableton AG. (2024). <em>Ableton Live 12 Reference Manual: MIDI Tools &amp; Clip View Design Standards</em>. Berlin: Ableton AG.","Cycling '74. (2024). <em>Max for Live MIDI Tools Guide: UI Design and Error Recovery</em>. San Francisco: Cycling '74.","Ableton AG. (2023). <em>Max for Live Production Guidelines: Live 12 Checklist - Tools</em>. Ableton Developer Documentation."],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8}],"exercises":[]}]};
